<title>FRANCE: EU 96/97 sugar output may exceed 16 mln tns - FIRS.</title>
<headline>EU 96/97 sugar output may exceed 16 mln tns - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union sugar output may slightly exceed 16 million tonnes white value in 1996/97, French sugar intervention board FIRS predicted on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In its January report, FIRS said that available EU data suggested a total EU output of 15.915 million tonnes for 1996/97 but that an expected increase in British production may lift that figure to slightly over 16 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This would compare with 15.560 million tonnes produced in 1995/96.</p>
<p>&quot;We however expect an upwards revision (by up to 100,000 tonnes) in UK output, which would bring EU beet sugar production to slightly over 16 million tonnes, above the previous record of 1992/94 (15,945 million tonnes),&quot; FIRS said.  </p>
<p>A European Union official has said the EU's sugar management committee may view new beet sugar production estimates on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
